XAAIsEasyPolygon compares the packed (x, y) vertices against the clip box,
which has to be packed the same way, and the stippled and tiled fills pass
XAAFillPolygonHelper the drawable origin packed, as it unpacks it with
intToX and intToY. The upstream commit

  613ce0955032fb032de0a3940752828d314f057a (master, xorg-server 1.6.0)
  f385303cd0242e3a7fded15f8b5c3d610c13ee41 (server-1.5-branch, 1.5.0)
  "Fix strict-aliasing silliness in XAA.", Adam Jackson, 2008-09-02

replaced *((int *)&extents->x1), *((int *)&extents->x2) and
*((int *)&pDraw->x) by the bare x shorts. Every vertex off row 0 then
looks clipped, so all FillPolygon calls go to miFillPolygon: XAA's polygon
fills and SubsequentSolidFillTrap have been unused since, and the stippled
and tiled fills would draw at a wrong drawable offset (x as y, x = 0 on
big-endian; y = 0 on little-endian). Pack them with coordToInt.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- a/hw/xfree86/xaa/xaaFillPoly.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/xaa/xaaFillPoly.c
@@ -123,8 +123,8 @@ XAAIsEasyPolygon(DDXPointPtr ptsIn, int
     *bottomY = 0;
 
     origin -= (origin & 0x8000) << 1;
-    vertex1 = extents->x1 - origin;
-    vertex2 = extents->x2 - origin /* - 0x00010001 */ ;
+    vertex1 = coordToInt(extents->x1, extents->y1) - origin;
+    vertex2 = coordToInt(extents->x2, extents->y2) - origin /* - 0x00010001 */ ;
     /* I think this was an error in cfb ^ */
 
     if (shape == Convex) {
@@ -727,7 +727,7 @@ XAAFillPolygonStippled(DrawablePtr pDraw
         return;
     }
 
-    origin = pDraw->x;
+    origin = coordToInt(pDraw->x, pDraw->y);
 
     switch (XAAIsEasyPolygon(ptsIn, count, &pGC->pCompositeClip->extents,
                              origin, &topPoint, &y, &maxy, shape)) {
@@ -887,7 +887,7 @@ XAAFillPolygonTiled(DrawablePtr pDraw,
         return;
     }
 
-    origin = pDraw->x;
+    origin = coordToInt(pDraw->x, pDraw->y);
 
     switch (XAAIsEasyPolygon(ptsIn, count, &pGC->pCompositeClip->extents,
                              origin, &topPoint, &y, &maxy, shape)) {
